 flooding is occurring and minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Pine Island Bayou near Sour Lake.\n\n* WHEN...Until Wednesday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 25.0 feet, Water inundates roads in lowland areas near\nthe river. Low spots on Old Sour Lake Road are under water.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 10:45 AM CDT Tuesday the stage was 26.7 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 22.0 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 10:45 AM CDT Tuesday was 27.0 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to fall below flood stage\ntomorrow morning and continue falling to 19.4 feet Sunday\nmorning.\n- Flood stage is 25.0 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 26.7\nfeet on 04/24/1977.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nMotorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.\n\nThe next statement will be issued this afternoon at 1215 PM CDT.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSLCH"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS84 KLCH 081601"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING NOW IN EFFECT UNTIL WEDNESDAY EVENING"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.EXT.KLCH.FL.W.0038.000000T0000Z-260910T0120Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-09-09T20:20:00-05:00"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.66d3e8e612c9823a635316d8a0fb694bb5e6edf3.002.1,2026-09-07T11:02:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d97ecdd49505fcad3982f9c9861fb9fa5dbd30d4.002.1,2026-09-06T20:11:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e56129b981fed12d0ac870d814d767501668755f.001.1,2026-09-06T10:17:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6726e7861c2669921792985f7e9b4df86b59cc51.001.1,2026-09-